{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389727-what-if-all-changelings-have-houses","id":1389727,"title":"What if all Changelings have Houses?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-18T12:35:35-07:00","id":1389727,"title":"What if all Changelings have Houses?","content":"So riddle me this. What if we changed it so all Changelings belong to a house, and specifically only those cast out of one are house less and they often join another house or sometimes become Dauntain. They don\u2019t necessarily have dots in nobility but at the very least they belong to a house. This would also open up the proliferation of Bannerhouses, or even just more houses in general. It\u2019s an interesting thing to consider, it makes it so Changeling can be a two axis splat like werewolf.<br /> <br /> I also see some ignoble houses, or clans for say Redcap corbies founded by an old chieftain in the days of yore, they have bare minimum nobles but they still have a house like structure. It could be an interesting houserule I may try someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T16:48:13-07:00","id":1389784,"title":"","content":"Yes I actually like that idea a lot. I might have to try this at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26140-whelan0kkult","name":"whelan0kkult","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:02:12-07:00","id":1389786,"title":"","content":"I've actually done that, usually combined with the idea that the Sidhe didn't leave and come back. It's usually worked pretty well.<br /> <br /> When I did it, I only used the original five Houses, plus the Scathach, with the idea of Fiona and Gwydion as the Seelie Houses (representing Spring and Summer, respectively), Dougal and Eiluned as the Unseelie Houses (representing Autumn and Winter), and Liam and Scathach as inbetweeners (representing the balance of Equinox and the extremes of the Solstice, respectively). It generally tended to work fairly well. Changelings who refuse to join or are kicked out of Houses were referred to as Pariahs.<br /> <br /> (In my head, such a set up would've had three two in one House books; Honor &amp; Passion, Shadow &amp; Steel, and Pain &amp; Sacrifice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:15:41-07:00","id":1389961,"title":"","content":"I don't personally go that far, I like the tension of the Nobility-Commoners as a theme too much, although I do see the appeal.<br /> <br /> I do use a similar idea though in that within Concordia, many changelings are at least nominally parts of houses in that they dwell within the domains held by the nobility of one house or another; outside of communes and outlaws and the like.<br /> <br /> So from the most gentle Boggan servant to the rowdiest Redcap hellraiser, if you live within a block of a city held by a Fiona Baronet, you may as well be considered Fiona for as far as the next Baronet over is concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:53:44-07:00","id":1389975,"title":"","content":"So would the end result be the de facto replacement of all the existing Changeling kingdoms with new &quot;kingdoms&quot; or realms based on each of the Houses? With each House being sovereign in whatever lands it controls? I would image such lands would not necessarily be contiguous, but with the &quot;world&quot; being a patchwork of baronies, counties,duchies, etc. like the old dynastic maps of Europe.<br /> <br /> In other words, it would be a world where it would be more correct to say &quot;This is the Realm of the Plantagenets. This is the Realm of the Capetians. This is the Realm of the Hohenstaufen.&quot; as opposed to this is the Kingdom of England, the Kingdom of France, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T10:18:01-07:00","id":1389999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389727-what-if-all-changelings-have-houses?p=1389961#post1389961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't personally go that far, I like the tension of the Nobility-Commoners as a theme too much, although I do see the appeal.<br /> <br /> I do use a similar idea though in that within Concordia, many changelings are at least nominally parts of houses in that they dwell within the domains held by the nobility of one house or another; outside of communes and outlaws and the like.<br /> <br /> So from the most gentle Boggan servant to the rowdiest Redcap hellraiser, if you live within a block of a city held by a Fiona Baronet, you may as well be considered Fiona for as far as the next Baronet over is concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But you still will have that. I am not saying all changelings are now noble, I am suggesting what if they all belonged to houses. Even with the current system you have the option to belong to a house but not be titled. Like with the resurgence the Sidhe brought with them retinue of Untitled House retainers of the commoner kiths that belonged to their houses but weren't nobles. Sadly the books didn't really cover what happened with these guys, I think they assumed they embraced the changeling way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389727-what-if-all-changelings-have-houses?p=1389975#post1389975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would the end result be the de facto replacement of all the existing Changeling kingdoms with new &quot;kingdoms&quot; or realms based on each of the Houses? With each House being sovereign in whatever lands it controls? I would image such lands would not necessarily be contiguous, but with the &quot;world&quot; being a patchwork of baronies, counties,duchies, etc. like the old dynastic maps of Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389727-what-if-all-changelings-have-houses?p=1389975#post1389975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In other words, it would be a world where it would be more correct to say &quot;This is the Realm of the Plantagenets. This is the Realm of the Capetians. This is the Realm of the Hohenstaufen.&quot; as opposed to this is the Kingdom of England, the Kingdom of France, and so on.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No the borders would be normal, its just now commoners would have a lot more clearly defined loyalties to specific houses.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T19:55:16-07:00","id":1390160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389727-what-if-all-changelings-have-houses?p=1389975#post1389975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would the end result be the de facto replacement of all the existing Changeling kingdoms with new &quot;kingdoms&quot; or realms based on each of the Houses? With each House being sovereign in whatever lands it controls? I would image such lands would not necessarily be contiguous, but with the &quot;world&quot; being a patchwork of baronies, counties,duchies, etc. like the old dynastic maps of Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was never a big fan of the Changeling political set up, especially with the whole &quot;Duchies = States/Provences&quot; part of it. So my Changeling games always tended to be a lot more chaotic, with a bunch of smaller kingdoms, fiefdoms, marches, city-states, confederations, and even the odd republic that heavily reflected local character and history. But when I did the &quot;everyone is in a House&quot; take, even places that didn't use any kind of nobility based system of governance would still have Houses, just with them being more like extended families or political parties, depending on the circumstances. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:12:50-07:00","id":1390183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1389727-what-if-all-changelings-have-houses?p=1390160#post1390160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was never a big fan of the Changeling political set up, especially with the whole &quot;Duchies = States/Provences&quot; part of it. So my Changeling games always tended to be a lot more chaotic, with a bunch of smaller kingdoms, fiefdoms, marches, city-states, confederations, and even the odd republic that heavily reflected local character and history. But when I did the &quot;everyone is in a House&quot; take, even places that didn't use any kind of nobility based system of governance would still have Houses, just with them being more like extended families or political parties, depending on the circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I like that take more, It doesn't make sense to me that we treat all the Kingdoms of the Kithain as belonging to one government... like what? And while I like the occasional by the will of the Dreaming Fiat, but by the time it gets to player's guide they go overboard with the amount of direct action the dreaming regularly takes to the point where it picks representatives if people don't pick them themselves, and it sets up the government for the Fae... not a fan of it just being handed to changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}